// TEST: Unannotated Triangular Literal Infers Symmetric
// The triangular shape IS `SymIdx<2, n>`'s storage — rows n, n-1, ..., 1 are
// exactly the left-justified simplex `canon_left_justify` addresses — so an
// unannotated nest of that profile infers the compact class rather than a
// ragged one. The reads are the assertion: R(1, 0) folds to the canonical
// (0, 1) and answers 2, where the ragged reading of the identical source would
// have given the short row's own first cell (4).
//
// The shape is genuinely shared with ragged data, so ragged data of THIS
// profile now carries its annotation (`RaggedIdx<lens>`, 019) — index-types
// 022/023/024/025 and the inference probes are the files that say so. Any
// other row profile is untouched: 232 pins that.
let R = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5], [6]]
let r10 = R(1, 0)
let r01 = R(0, 1)
let r11 = R(1, 1)
let r22 = R(2, 2)
// EXPECT: R = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5], [6]]
// EXPECT: r10 = 2
// EXPECT: r01 = 2
// EXPECT: r11 = 4
// EXPECT: r22 = 6
